# Scheduled work for the shared deployment. Install to /etc/cron.d/anvil-cron, root-owned, 0644.
#
# ONE DEPLOYMENT, ONE CALL PER JOB. This replaces the control-plane dispatcher, which existed
# because every clan was its own container and something had to know the list. It is not merely
# unnecessary now — it is harmful. Every one of these endpoints already sweeps the whole database
# and derives each row's clan from the row, so fanning out per clan would run the SAME global sweep
# once per clan: N concurrent passes over the same accounts, all of them hitting the Jagex hiscores.
#
# The poll budget is the scarce resource in this system. Keeping it to one call is the whole point.
#
# Cadence matches what the dispatcher used to stagger:
#   flush-notifications  every minute   — the debounce backstop, plus scheduled start/end posts
#   stats                every 15 min   — the hiscores sweep; self-limiting (oldest-first, bounded)
#   weekly               every 15 min   — competition lifecycle: enrol, flip status, announce
#   backup               daily          — pg_dump to object storage
#
# Staggering is by minute offset rather than by a queue: stats and weekly both want the quarter
# hour, and running them in the same second means the weekly enrolment races the sweep that is about
# to read it.

SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

* * * * *      root /opt/anvil/site-cron.sh flush-notifications
2,17,32,47 * * * * root /opt/anvil/site-cron.sh stats
5,20,35,50 * * * * root /opt/anvil/site-cron.sh weekly
17 4 * * *     root /opt/anvil/site-cron.sh backup
